npm-debug.log*

# ---- Capacitor native projects -------------------------------------------
# android/ and ios/ ARE committed, deliberately. `npx cap add` scaffolds them
# once; from then on `cap sync` only copies the web build and refreshes plugin
# references, and never rewrites AndroidManifest.xml or build.gradle. Those
# files carry real configuration — the portrait lock, the Android 11+ <queries>
# block that outbound links depend on, versionName, the release signing hook —
# so regenerating them from scratch would silently ship a different app.
#
# Each native project brings its own .gitignore for the machine-specific and
# generated parts (build/, .gradle/, local.properties, the copied web assets in
# app/src/main/assets/public, capacitor.config.json). Those stay out; the source
# of the project goes in. See ANDROID.md.
android/local.properties
android/capacitor.build.gradle
android/app/capacitor.build.gradle
android/.idea/
local.properties
.gradle/

# ---- JVM crash dumps ------------------------------------------------------
# A JVM writes these into its working directory, which for the VS Code Java
# language server is the workspace root — so a crash litters this folder with a
# ~45 KB hs_err and a ~300 KB replay file. They are machine-specific diagnostics,
# never source. Delete them once read.
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log

# ---- Release signing ------------------------------------------------------
# Never commit a keystore or its passwords. The app has never been published, so
# it auto-enrols in Play App Signing on first upload and bagga-fitness.jks is
# the UPLOAD key — losing it costs a Play Console reset request, not the
# listing. Back it up anyway, and keep it outside this tree: these rules stop it
# being committed, they do not stop `git clean -xfd` or `git stash -a` deleting
# it. See the Release signing section of ANDROID.md.
*.keystore
*.jks
keystore.properties
key.properties

# ---- Local scratch --------------------------------------------------------
# Throwaway harnesses used to build and eyeball generated art: standalone
# render scripts, their esbuild output, and the PNG/SVG sheets they produce.
# The art they were used to author lives in src/components/art/ and IS
# committed; these are the scaffolding, kept on disk because re-deriving a pose
# by hand is slow, and ignored because they are megabytes of regenerable output
# that would otherwise sit in every `git status` forever.
#
# Note the asymmetry with the keystore rules above: because these are ignored,
# `git clean -fd` now leaves them alone — but `git clean -xfd` still deletes
# them, and unlike tracked files there is no copy in history to restore from.
.tmp-*
mmcheck/
